@event crisis_collapse
# en: Collapse
title [59ccfe] = 倒下
# en: The world tilts. When it rights itself you are in the infirmary, and Sister Amaranth is looking at you over her spectacles. "You have been running your body like a borrowed broom," she says.
text [f87609] = 世界倾斜了。等它恢复正常时，你已经躺在医务室里，阿玛兰斯修女正从眼镜上方看着你。“你对待自己的身体，就像对待一把借来的飞帚。”她说。
# en: A narrow infirmary bed under a high arched window, a healer's lamp floating beside it.
scene [27d146] = 高高的拱窗下一张窄窄的病床，旁边悬浮着一盏治疗师的灯。
# en: Pay for the full cure (30 gold)
opt.left.label [97a3e9] = 付钱彻底治好（30 金币）
# en: Three foul tonics and two days' sleep later, you feel almost human.
opt.left.say.1 [ecd52f] = 三剂难喝的药和两天的睡眠之后，你感觉差不多像个人了。
# en: Ask to rest instead
opt.right.label [8eabcd] = 请求静养
# en: A long, dull fortnight in bed. Sister Amaranth warns you: "Next time, I write to your family."
opt.right.say.1 [b20134] = 在床上躺了漫长而无聊的两周。阿玛兰斯修女警告你：“下次，我就写信给你家里。”

@event crisis_despair
# en: The Grey
title [9c424f] = 灰色
# en: Your spirits have hit bottom. Everything has gone grey: food tastes of nothing, lectures are noise, and you have packed your trunk twice this week and unpacked it once. It would be so easy to take the next barge and simply stop.
text [2115ba] = 你的心情跌到了谷底。一切都变成了灰色：吃什么都没味道，课堂只剩噪音，这周你收拾了两次行李，又拆开了一次。坐上下一班驳船，就此停下，是多么容易。
# en: A student sitting on the edge of a dormitory bed, rain on the window, a packed trunk by the door.
scene [dc74cf] = 一个学生坐在宿舍床沿，窗上有雨，门边放着收拾好的行李箱。
# en: Reach out to someone
opt.left.label [e2c5e9] = 向别人伸出手
# en: Spirits come back, after a night that breaks something else.
opt.left.hint [b0fa2b] = 心情会回来，但要先熬过一个毁掉别的东西的夜晚。
# en: First you cry, properly, the way you haven't since you were small, until the window goes pale. Then you sleep straight through the morning's lectures, and wake ashamed of it.
opt.left.say.1 [818977] = 你先是哭，痛痛快快地哭，像小时候那样，一直哭到窗外发白。然后你一觉睡过了上午所有的课，醒来时满心羞愧。
# en: You walk out to the empty practice field and cast until there is nothing left to cast: fire, wind, light, anything. You come back hollow and shaking, and lighter.
opt.left.say.2 [0e034a] = 你走到空荡荡的练习场，一直施法，直到再也施不出任何东西：火、风、光，什么都行。回来时你空空荡荡、浑身发抖，却轻松了。
# en: You walk the grounds in the rain all night without a cloak, round and round the lawns. A prefect finds you at dawn, soaked to the skin, and the story is round the dormitory by breakfast.
opt.left.say.3 [ddf53e] = 你没披斗篷，在雨里绕着草坪走了一整夜。黎明时一个级长发现了你，浑身湿透，早饭前这事就传遍了宿舍。
# en: You throw your inkwell at the wall, then the chair, then the little mirror. Afterwards you sit among the pieces, oddly calm. Replacing it all costs a small fortune.
opt.left.say.4 [6262b2] = 你把墨水瓶砸向墙，然后是椅子，然后是那面小镜子。之后你坐在一地碎片中间，出奇地平静。把这些东西全部换新，花了一小笔钱。
# en: In the morning you knock on a friend's door. They don't ask questions. They just make tea, and stay.
opt.left.say.5 [ddca3a] = 早上你敲响了朋友的门。对方什么也没问。只是泡了茶，陪着你。
# en: Old Maud finds you in the gardens and puts a trowel in your hand. "Dig," she says. You dig. It helps more than it should.
opt.left.say.6 [a27142] = 老莫德在花园里找到你，把一把小铲子塞进你手里。“挖。”她说。你挖了。这比想象中更有用。
# en: Afterwards you talk to the night porter, of all people. He tells you about his own first year. It's enough, for now.
opt.left.say.7 [ae8ca6] = 事后你竟然和守夜门房聊了起来。他给你讲了他自己的一年级。暂时，这就够了。
# en: Take the next barge
opt.right.label [c52bdf] = 坐下一班驳船
# en: Spirits back for now; a second time, you go.
opt.right.hint [e4dad5] = 心情暂时回来；第二次，你就会离开。
# en: You get as far as the landing. The barge is late. By the time it arrives, you have decided to stay one more month.
opt.right.say.1 [d9e779] = 你走到了码头。驳船晚点了。等它到的时候，你决定再留一个月。

@event crisis_probation
# en: The Disciplinary Board
title [f764c3] = 纪律委员会
# en: Two terms of failing marks. You are summoned before the Disciplinary Board: three professors and the headmistress, who looks at you with an expression of deep, patient disappointment. {flag(board_reprieve): They have seen you here before.|}
text [db6aa2] = 连续两个学期挂科。你被传唤到纪律委员会面前：三位教授和院长，院长看着你的表情里满是深沉而耐心的失望。{flag(board_reprieve): 他们以前在这里见过你。|}
# en: Three professors behind a high bench in a dim chamber, the headmistress in the centre, hands folded.
scene [e88ce4] = 昏暗的厅堂里，三位教授坐在高高的长桌后，院长居中，双手交握。
# en: Plead your case
opt.left.label [bb8fcc] = 为自己辩护
# en: You speak honestly and well. They grant you one reprieve, and a study plan that fills every evening. "There will not be a second," says the headmistress, pleasantly.
opt.left.say.1 [03505f] = 你说得诚恳而得体。他们给了你一次宽限，还有一份把每个晚上都排满的学习计划。“不会有第二次了，”院长和气地说。
# en: Promise to work harder
opt.right.label [a78172] = 保证会更努力
# en: "Promises are cheap," says Professor Thorne. "We'll take this one. Only this one." A reprieve, a study plan in his own hand, and a very long term ahead.
opt.right.say.1 [8df15e] = “承诺不值钱，”索恩教授说，“这一次我们收下。只此一次。”一次宽限，一份他亲笔写的学习计划，以及一个漫长的学期。

@event grisk_reminder
# en: A Friendly Reminder
title [6aaed3] = 友情提醒
# en: A note on your door, in a tidy goblin hand: "A payment was missed. Mister Grisk is a patient businessman. Mister Grisk charges interest on his patience." Underneath, smaller: "Pay something, or another month will be added."
text [67613b] = 你门上钉着一张字条，是工整的地精笔迹：“有一笔还款逾期了。格里斯克先生是位有耐心的生意人。格里斯克先生的耐心是要收利息的。”下面一行小字：“多少还一点，否则再加一个月。”
# en: A small, very neat note pinned to a dormitory door with a brass tack, the handwriting tiny and precise.
scene [309f11] = 一张小小的、非常整洁的字条用黄铜图钉钉在宿舍门上，字迹细小而一丝不苟。
# en: Scrape together what you can
opt.left.label [d226e0] = 能凑多少凑多少
# en: You empty your purse into an envelope and slide it under his door. It isn't twelve crowns. It is, says the note in reply, "a gesture. Noted."
opt.left.say.1 [acdacd] = 你把钱袋倒进一个信封，塞到他门下。不到十二克朗。回信的字条上写着：“一份心意。已记录。”
# en: There is nothing to put in the envelope. You write "next month, I promise" on a scrap and slide that under his door instead. The reply is a single line, "Promises are added to the ledger," and another month is.
opt.left.say.2 [b418a0] = 信封里没什么可放的。你在一张纸片上写下“下个月，我保证”，从他门缝底下塞了进去。回信只有一行：“承诺记入账簿。”账簿上又多了一个月。
# en: Put it out of your mind
opt.right.label [68419d] = 别去想它
# en: You put the note in a drawer. Another month goes on the ledger, and next month the knock on your door will be louder.
opt.right.say.1 [2bdb82] = 你把字条塞进抽屉。账本上又多了一个月，下个月的敲门声会更响。

@event grisk_collectors
# en: Grisk's Collectors
title [eb1401] = 格里斯克的讨债人
# en: Two trolls in waistcoats are waiting outside your dormitory. "Mister Grisk," says the larger one, "is disappointed." The smaller one cracks his knuckles, which sounds like a rockslide.
text [6dfc11] = 两个穿马甲的巨魔等在你的宿舍外。“格里斯克先生，”大个子说，“很失望。”小个子把指关节捏得咔咔响，听起来像山崩。
# en: Two large trolls in ill-fitting waistcoats looming in a dormitory doorway, one holding a ledger.
scene [8592b2] = 两个穿着不合身马甲的高大巨魔堵在宿舍门口，其中一个拿着账簿。
# en: Hand over everything you have
opt.left.label [eec2ea] = 交出所有的钱
# en: They count your purse twice and declare the debt settled. "Pleasure," says the large one, meaning it.
opt.left.say.1 [377b97] = 他们把你的钱袋数了两遍，宣布债务两清。“荣幸。”大个子说，是真心的。
# en: They take every coin and your good boots, in front of half the corridor. "Partial," they say, and leave.
opt.left.say.2 [8315e9] = 他们当着半条走廊的人，拿走了每一枚硬币和你最好的靴子。“部分还款。”他们说完就走了。
# en: Run
opt.right.label [57e66a] = 逃跑
# en: You escape across the rooftops. They'll be back, but not this month.
opt.right.say.1 [24257a] = 你从屋顶上逃走了。他们还会回来，但不是这个月。
# en: You do not escape. The trolls are surprisingly gentle about breaking only one rib.
opt.right.say.2 [0374eb] = 你没逃掉。巨魔们出人意料地温柔，只断了你一根肋骨。
